+// The protocol proposed 2300h/2301h (docs/rom-pico-protocol.md 2, 7 item 1), on
+// the grounds that o1-memory-io-map.md 7 calls 2300-23FF the largest clean
+// block.  It is not clean, and the reason is in this driver: the onboard selects
+// check only two address bits, so 2300h/2301h are also the floppy controller's
+// command/status and track registers and the keyboard's row 0 -- measured, and
+// recorded in docs/o1-mainboard-schematic.md 7a ("0x2301 is keyboard *and*
+// floppy", from tools/o1_mame_probe.lua's C9 report).  A reply register ANDed
+// with the FDC's track register -- 0x00 at the sign-on -- reads "not ready" for
+// ever, and a request written to 2300h is a floppy command.
+//
+// 2800h is inside the block o1-memory-io-map.md 7 recommends (2300-28FF) and is
+// the part of it nothing selects: no device mask matches A11 set with A8/A9/A10
+// clear, so the stock decode reads 0xFF there and the door answers alone.  The
+// rest of that region is not free either -- 2400h-27FF is the SCREEN-PAC's own
+// decode, presence bit included (2400h, bit 2 LOW = fitted), which the video
+// personality needs.
